    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68698" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μον-όφθαλμος</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μουν-</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one-eyed</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.116
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				2.1.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				18.9
			</span></i>: rejected by <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				112
			</span></i>; expld. as <i>one who has one eye</i>, like
			the Cyclops, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτερόφθαλμος</span>,
				<i>one who has lost an eye</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ammon.
				<u>Diff.</u>
				p.60
			</span></i> V.</div>
